win32u: Draw caption buttons and the outer frame flat.

The caption buttons were Marlett glyphs on a 3D push button, and the outer edge was a raised or sunken DrawEdge,
which put white and light gray lines around the window. The buttons now have no fill and no frame in the normal
state. Their glyphs are 1 px lines, 40 percent of the button height, in RGB(170,170,170). Pressed, a button shows a
rounded RGB(75,75,75) fill with a white glyph, and close shows RGB(196,43,28). The outer edge is a solid ring in the
ActiveBorder or InactiveBorder colour, with the same width as before. Button rectangles, hit testing and the title
bar height do not change.

